  "description": "QEPTOX crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 2/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C92 H116 Dy4 O32,C92 H116 Dy4 O32. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.731-3.860 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 103.93-109.03°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C92H116Dy4O32. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
